[2026-06-15T19:25:39.819Z] [STDOUT] Fixes https://github.com/link-assistant/formal-ai/issues/488

## Summary
- Add a default assistant thinking preview that is visible outside diagnostics mode, with collapsed current/previous steps and an expandable ordered list.
- Naturalize structured solver steps into localized user-facing summaries while keeping raw `.thinking-steps` and diagnostics panels behind diagnostics mode.
- Add a `Thinking detail` setting (`brief`, `standard`, `detailed`) that reshapes existing previews from the same structured trace.
- Add the Issue #488 case study with raw research/check logs and a verification screenshot.

## Screenshot
![Expanded thinking preview](https://github.com/link-assistant/formal-ai/blob/issue-488-54ea7213044c/docs/case-studies/issue-488/screenshots/thinking-preview-expanded.png?raw=true)

## Reproduction
- Added `tests/e2e/tests/issue-488.spec.js`; before the fix it failed because `[data-testid="thinking-preview"]` was missing for completed assistant messages when diagnostics mode was off.

## Tests
- `npm --prefix tests/e2e run check:i18n`
- `npm --prefix tests/e2e run check:web-tdz`
- `npm --prefix tests/e2e run test:local -- --grep "Issue #488"`
- `npm --prefix tests/e2e run test:local -- --grep "diagnostics toggle shows trace"`
- `rust-script scripts/check-file-size.rs`
- `cargo fmt --check`
- `cargo clippy --all-targets --all-features`
- `cargo test`

